        <mxCell id="c46" value="Anomaly columns, outside the register" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="72" width="280" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c47" value="&lt;i&gt;The model answer&#x27;s queries, left to right (the Power Query editor&#x27;s names). Applications grouped two ways, the credit memos and the refunds feed the two flag queries, which are tables of the model (hidden); each flag pair is unpivoted into an exception query that does not load, and the register appends those with Chapter 16&#x27;s three, then merges the dispositions and the design findings. Its TestID is related to the Tests table, whose Process (Credit memos or Refunds) the Population measure reads: a process spelled differently leaves the population and the rate blank while the exceptions still count. MethodMismatch and OffsetMissed are columns of the refund table only, read by their own measures and page.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="502" width="860" height="83" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
